# INBOUND READ RECEIPTS — iMessage provider

## 0. Verification pass — what checks out, and 5 corrections

**Confirmed exactly as stated:** upstream `message.read` shape (`node_modules/@photon-ai/advanced-imessage/dist/groups-CYV3GKtn.d.ts:626-641`, `readAt: Date` non-optional, `actor?` optional); the catch-all at `packages/imessage/src/remote/stream.ts:156-160`; `isEventFromCurrentAccount` at `:56-63`; `isMessageEvent` prefix match at `:221-222`; `skipUnmappable` at `:79-103`; `clientStream`/`messages` at `:383-401`/`:444-475`; `resolveReactionTarget` at `packages/imessage/src/remote/reactions.ts:58-85` (private, bare `catch { return; }`); `toReactionMessages` at `:87-130`; `buildMessageBase` direction at `packages/imessage/src/remote/inbound.ts:124`; `cacheRemoteOutbound` at `packages/imessage/src/index.ts:112-131`; `wrapNestedContent` arms at `packages/core/src/platform/build.ts:536-598` with the `edit` arm at `:570-584` and the bare `return content` at `:597`; `rawDirection` honored at `:483-488`/`:507`; `mapContent` at `packages/core/src/webhook/deserialize.ts:125-174` with `buildTargetRecord` at `:295-309`; `FIRE_AND_FORGET_TYPES` containing `"read"` at `build.ts:66`; `configSchema` strictObject at `packages/imessage/src/types.ts:25-27`; `test/config.test.ts:6` asserting `parse({})` → `{}`.

**Corrections / additions:**

1. **`readSchema` is NOT exported from `@spectrum-ts/core/authoring`.** `packages/core/src/authoring.ts:53` exports only `asRead`, and `asRead(input: { target: Message })` will not accept a raw `IMessageMessage` record. This is a required one-line core change that the brief missed. Precedent for the fix is right above it: `reactionSchema` is exported at `authoring.ts:52`, `replySchema` at `:55`, `groupSchema` at `:44`.

2. **"reaches the app as an UNWRAPPED raw record (no `space`)" is imprecise, and the truth is worse.** The raw record *does* carry `space: { id, type, phone }` and `timestamp: Date` and `direction: "outbound"`. So without the `wrapNestedContent` arm, `message.content.target` would be a structurally *plausible-looking* object that silently lacks `.reply()`, `.react()`, `.edit()`, `.unsend()`, `.platform`, `.extras`, and a real `Space` — a type lie rather than an obvious absence. Strengthens the case for the arm; weakens any "ship without it" option.

3. **`config.test.ts` does not actually need updating.** Zod v4 `.optional()` omits absent keys from the output object, which is exactly why `parse({})` already deep-equals `{}` today despite `clients` existing. Adding `readReceipts: z.boolean().optional()` keeps that green. We should still *add* tests there.

4. **`messages.subscribeEvents(filter?)` only supports `{ chat?: string }`** (`node_modules/@photon-ai/advanced-imessage/dist/grpc.d.ts:219-221`). There is no server-side event-type filter, so the opt-in cannot save bandwidth — `message.read` frames arrive on the wire either way. The flag gates consumer-visible volume and RPC/CPU cost only. Worth saying out loud in the plan so nobody expects a network win.

5. **There is no outbound `read` Message today, so `direction` is not currently load-bearing for disambiguation.** `"read"` is in `FIRE_AND_FORGET_TYPES` (`build.ts:66`), so `dispatchSend` returns `undefined` (`build.ts:658-663`) and `space.send(read(msg))` never produces a Message. `case "read":` on `app.messages` is *today* unambiguously inbound. The `direction === "inbound"` guard is still the right thing to write and document — it is the stable contract — but the plan should not claim it currently discriminates two live cases.

Two more things I verified that materially shape the design:

6. **Self-sent messages are never cached by the stream.** `stream.ts:121-123` early-returns `message.received` with `isFromMe: true` *before* any rebuild/cache. So the message cache is populated with our outbound messages **only** by `cacheRemoteOutbound` at send time. Consequence: after a process restart, read receipts for pre-restart sends will always miss the cache and pay an RPC. This is the single most important input to the cache-miss question below.

7. **The message stream is strictly serial.** `resumable-stream.ts:384-385` and `:422` do `await deliverItem(await options.processLive(event), …)` in a `for await`. Any RPC inside `toMessageItem` head-of-line-blocks real inbound messages on that line.

