1. **`docs/content/read.mdx.vel`** (new — there is no `read` page today, even though outbound `read()` has shipped). Outbound half mirrors `docs/content/unsend.mdx.vel`; inbound half mirrors `docs/content/membership.mdx.vel:35-63`. Per-platform granularity table is already written in the JSDoc at `packages/core/src/content/read.ts:17-26`. The `## Inbound read receipts` section states: `sender` is the reader; `target` is the message *you* sent (`direction: "outbound"`, so `.edit()`/`.unsend()` work on it); `timestamp` is when it was read, not observed; **one message per reader in a group**; and `case "read":` on `app.messages` is always a receipt — outbound `read` is fire-and-forget and produces no Message, so no direction check is needed.
