{"body":"### Shared mode misattributes read receipts

**High Severity**

<!-- DESCRIPTION START -->
`toReader` trusts `actor` whenever `actor.address !== phone`. In shared mode `phone` is the `"shared"` sentinel, so the verified real-world shape — `actor` naming our own pool line — always passes that check and never falls through to `dmPeerFromChatGuid`. Every DM receipt then surfaces with the agent as `message.sender` instead of the peer. `isActorCurrentAccount` already treats the sentinel as non-matching for this reason.
<!-- DESCRIPTION END -->

